## Method (per test)
1. Run the test, read the assertion. `git log -p 4bad5ac979..HEAD -- <files the test reads>` to find the campaign commit that changed the
   checked artifact (runner script, sample source, docs, shared runner `redis-common.sh` — e.g. `8e76335988` moved cleanup ownership into
   `redis-common.sh`, `9a0371fea7`/`stage2-sample-runners-report-sigkill` changed runner reporting).
2. Decide which side drifted: (a) the sample/runner/doc lost something the test rightly guards (health checks use location readiness,
   isolated Docker redis per runner, client+server evidence, entry-owned actor destroy, DeliveryDispatch common role model) → restore it at
   the owner; (b) the test asserts the *old shape* of an intentionally consolidated runner (one cleanup owner in `redis-common.sh`) → update the
   test to check the invariant through the new owner (the invariant itself stays; do not delete the check). Record which for each test with
   the commit hash that caused it.
3. Never weaken an invariant; never add a runner-local duplicate of something `redis-common.sh` now owns.

